Subject:  U.S. House of Representatives WWW home page
Date: Thu, 26 Jan 1995 17:08:35
Message-ID: <DCM.129.0011252B@hr.house.gov>


The U.S. House of Representatives has a World Wide Web server online.

The Server contains, among other things, floor schedules, names, addresses
and internet addresses of members, pointers to member office gophers,
a searchable 1993 U.S. Code (the 94 code will be out soon), text of
pending legislation, and the internet law library.

(The internet law library is a  www page containing links to ALL of the 
legal resources on the internet in the world.)

The URL for the site is: http://www.house.gov

btw, there is a link to send comments and suggestions. if you have any
comments or suggestions or hints about how it can be added to or improved,
please let us know.

Thanks for any time you can spare,
dave massie
